  "id": "osf-symlink-resolution",
  "generatedAt": "2026-10-06T13:24:09.918Z",
  "title": "Symlink resolution in osf check and scan",
  "summary": "Adds a shared `symlink` module that decides what a symlink means to the scanner. A link whose real target lives inside the repository is now followed to the files behind it, so `check scan`, `lint-writing` and `lint-skill` see the real content instead of counting the link as excluded; a link that points outside the repository, into `.git`, at nothing, or in a loop is refused with a `symlink refused:` error that names the link. `check.rs` expands links before its existence check, and `scan`'s directory walk now emits `(label, real)` pairs so a file reached through a link is read from its real path but reported under the path as walked.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
